concepts.body:
Every website and app runs on computers somewhere. You already know a **server**: a computer that is always on and reachable over the internet. Companies used to buy their own and keep them in a back room. Today most rent them from a **cloud provider**, a company such as Amazon Web Services (AWS), Microsoft Azure or Google Cloud that owns huge buildings full of computers and rents out pieces of them by the hour.

Renting computing this way is called the **cloud**. A rented server is usually a **virtual machine**: a complete computer simulated in software, one of many sharing a real machine. You can have one running in a minute and delete it when you're done.

The things you rent are called **resources**, and together they make up your **infrastructure**: the foundation your app stands on, like the plumbing and wiring of a building.

Common resources:

- virtual machines, to run programs;
- storage **buckets**: online folders for files, such as photos your users upload;
- **databases**: organised stores of data, such as customer accounts;
- private networks that connect your machines and keep strangers out;
- user accounts and permissions saying who may do what.

Websites also need **DNS** records. DNS is the internet's address book: it turns a name like `shop.example.com` into the numeric address of your server.

Each cloud provider runs its machines in several **regions**, groups of buildings in one part of the world, such as Ireland (`eu-west-1`) or Virginia (`us-east-1`). You pick regions close to your users.

There are two ways to create resources. People click through the cloud company's web console, a website for managing the account. Programs use its **API**: a fixed menu of instructions a program can send, like "create a bucket named photos", which the company's computers then carry out.

Every instruction must prove who sent it. The cloud company gives you **credentials**, such as an access key (a long secret password meant for programs), and only accepts instructions that carry valid ones. Guard them like house keys: anyone holding them can create, change or delete what you rent, and you get the bill.

concepts.code:
# main.tf: the whole idea in one resource
terraform {
  required_providers {              # which providers to download
    aws = { source = "hashicorp/aws", version = "~> 6.0" }
  }
}

provider "aws" {
  region = "eu-west-1"              # Ireland
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "logs" {   # a storage bucket in AWS (S3 is AWS's file storage)
  bucket = "acme-app-logs-prod"     # the bucket's name
}
# terraform init   -> downloads the AWS provider
# terraform plan   -> Plan: 1 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy.
# terraform apply  -> aws_s3_bucket.logs: Creation complete

terraform {
  required_version = ">= 1.10"      # which Terraform versions may run this
  required_providers {
    aws    = { source = "hashicorp/aws", version = "~> 6.0" }
    random = { source = "hashicorp/random", version = "~> 3.7" }
  }
}

provider "aws" {
  region = "eu-west-1"
  default_tags { tags = { team = "platform", managed_by = "terraform" } }   # labels on everything
}

provider "aws" {
  alias  = "us"
  region = "us-east-1"              # a second region, used only where asked
}
# terraform init
# - Installing hashicorp/aws v6.x.y...
# Terraform has created a lock file .terraform.lock.hcl

variable "environment" {
  type        = string
  description = "Deployment environment"
}

variable "instance" {
  type = object({
    type  = string
    count = optional(number, 1)          # may be left out; then 1
  })
  default = { type = "t3.small" }
}

output "summary" {
  value = "${var.environment}: ${var.instance.count} x ${var.instance.type}"   # ${} inserts values
}
# prod.tfvars:   environment = "prod"
#                instance    = { type = "m7i.large", count = 3 }
# terraform apply -var-file=prod.tfvars
# summary = "prod: 3 x m7i.large"
# TF_VAR_environment=dev terraform plan     # value from an environment variable

data "aws_caller_identity" "current" {}    # who am I signed in as?

data "aws_ami" "ubuntu" {
  most_recent = true
  owners      = ["099720109477"]          # Canonical, the makers of Ubuntu
  filter {
    name   = "name"
    values = ["ubuntu/images/hvm-ssd-gp3/ubuntu-noble-24.04-amd64-server-*"]
  }
}

data "aws_iam_policy_document" "read_logs" {
  statement {                             # allow reading files in one bucket
    actions   = ["s3:GetObject"]
    resources = ["arn:aws:s3:::acme-app-logs-prod/*"]
  }
}

output "account" { value = data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id }
output "ami"     { value = data.aws_ami.ubuntu.id }

variable "env" {
  type    = string
  default = "prod"
}

variable "users" {
  type = list(object({ name = string, admin = bool }))
  default = [
    { name = "ana", admin = true },
    { name = "bo", admin = false },
  ]
}

locals {                     # named values used below (locals come in Practical)
  replicas = var.env == "prod" ? 3 : 1
  admins   = [for u in var.users : u.name if u.admin]
  by_name  = { for u in var.users : u.name => u.admin }
}

output "replicas" { value = local.replicas } # 3
output "admins"   { value = local.admins }   # ["ana"]
output "by_name"  { value = local.by_name }  # { ana = true, bo = false }

variable "env" {
  type    = string
  default = "prod"
}

locals {
  name_prefix = "acme-${var.env}"
  common_tags = merge({ env = var.env, managed_by = "terraform" }, { team = "platform" })
  azs         = ["eu-west-1a", "eu-west-1b", "eu-west-1c"]
  subnets     = { for i, az in local.azs : az => cidrsubnet("10.0.0.0/16", 8, i) }
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version   = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{ Effect = "Allow", Action = ["s3:GetObject"], Resource = "*" }]
  })
}

output "subnets" { value = local.subnets }
# { "eu-west-1a" = "10.0.0.0/24", "eu-west-1b" = "10.0.1.0/24", "eu-west-1c" = "10.0.2.0/24" }
output "team" { value = lookup(local.common_tags, "team", "none") }   # "platform"

variable "users" {
  type    = set(string)
  default = ["ana", "bo", "cy"]
}

variable "create_bastion" {
  type    = bool
  default = false
}

resource "terraform_data" "user" {
  for_each = var.users                # address: terraform_data.user["bo"]
  input    = "user-${each.key}"
}

resource "terraform_data" "bastion" {
  count = var.create_bastion ? 1 : 0  # conditional resource
  input = "bastion"
}

output "user_inputs" { value = [for u in terraform_data.user : u.output] }
# ["user-ana", "user-bo", "user-cy"]
# Removing "ana" later destroys only terraform_data.user["ana"].

resource "aws_launch_template" "app" {
  name_prefix   = "app-"                      # unique names allow overlap
  image_id      = var.ami_id
  instance_type = "t3.small"
  lifecycle { create_before_destroy = true }
}

resource "aws_db_instance" "main" {
  identifier        = "shop-prod"
  engine            = "postgres"
  instance_class    = "db.t4g.medium"
  allocated_storage = 50
  lifecycle {
    prevent_destroy = true
    ignore_changes  = [allocated_storage]     # storage autoscaling grows it
  }
}

resource "aws_ecs_service" "app" {
  name       = "app"
  depends_on = [aws_iam_role_policy.app]      # hidden ordering requirement
  # ... task_definition, cluster, desired_count ...
}

# modules/bucket/main.tf
variable "name" { type = string }
variable "versioning" {
  type    = bool
  default = true
}
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "this" { bucket = var.name }
resource "aws_s3_bucket_versioning" "this" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.this.id
  versioning_configuration { status = var.versioning ? "Enabled" : "Suspended" }
}
output "arn" { value = aws_s3_bucket.this.arn }

# envs/prod/main.tf
module "logs" {
  source = "../../modules/bucket"
  name   = "acme-logs-prod"
}
output "logs_arn" { value = module.logs.arn }
# address in state: module.logs.aws_s3_bucket.this

variable "networks" {
  default = {
    app  = { subnets = ["a", "b"] }
    data = { subnets = ["a"] }
  }
}

locals {
  subnet_list = flatten([
    for net, cfg in var.networks : [
      for s in cfg.subnets : { network = net, name = s }
    ]
  ])
  subnets = { for s in local.subnet_list : "${s.network}.${s.name}" => s }
}

resource "terraform_data" "subnet" {
  for_each = local.subnets               # keys: app.a, app.b, data.a
  input    = "${each.value.network}-${each.value.name}"
}
output "keys" { value = keys(local.subnets) }   # ["app.a", "app.b", "data.a"]

# 1. Renamed a resource and moved it into a module
moved {
  from = aws_s3_bucket.logs
  to   = module.logs.aws_s3_bucket.this
}

# 2. Adopt a bucket created by hand
import {
  to = aws_s3_bucket.legacy
  id = "acme-legacy-bucket"
}
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "legacy" { bucket = "acme-legacy-bucket" }

# 3. Hand an instance over to another team's config without deleting it
removed {
  from = aws_instance.reporting
  lifecycle { destroy = false }
}
# terraform plan
#   # aws_s3_bucket.logs has moved to module.logs.aws_s3_bucket.this
#   # aws_s3_bucket.legacy will be imported
#   # aws_instance.reporting will no longer be managed by Terraform

variable "env" {
  type = string
  validation {
    condition     = contains(["dev", "staging", "prod"], var.env)
    error_message = "env must be dev, staging or prod."
  }
}

variable "bucket_name" {
  type = string
  validation {
    condition     = can(regex("^[a-z0-9.-]{3,63}$", var.bucket_name))
    error_message = "Bucket names: 3-63 chars of a-z, 0-9, dots and hyphens."
  }
}

resource "terraform_data" "bucket" {
  input = var.bucket_name
  lifecycle {
    postcondition {
      condition     = startswith(self.output, var.env)
      error_message = "Bucket name must start with the environment name."
    }
  }
}

# tests/bucket.tftest.hcl  (module from the modules lesson)
mock_provider "aws" {}

variables {
  name = "acme-logs-test"
}

run "versioning_enabled_by_default" {
  command = plan
  assert {
    condition     = aws_s3_bucket_versioning.this.versioning_configuration[0].status == "Enabled"
    error_message = "Versioning should default to Enabled"
  }
}

run "can_disable_versioning" {
  variables { versioning = false }
  assert {
    condition     = aws_s3_bucket_versioning.this.versioning_configuration[0].status == "Suspended"
    error_message = "versioning = false should suspend versioning"
  }
}
# terraform test
# tests/bucket.tftest.hcl... pass  (2 passed, 0 failed)

terraform providers
# Providers required by configuration:
# ├── provider[registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/aws] ~> 6.0
# └── module.vpc
#     └── provider[registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/aws] >= 6.0

terraform providers lock -platform=linux_amd64 -platform=darwin_arm64
terraform providers mirror /opt/tf-mirror        # for air-gapped installs
terraform providers schema -json | jq '.provider_schemas | keys'

# ~/.terraformrc
# provider_installation {
#   filesystem_mirror { path = "/opt/tf-mirror" }
#   direct { exclude = ["registry.terraform.io/*/*"] }
# }

variable "db_password" {
  type      = string
  sensitive = true
  ephemeral = true                 # never stored in state or plan
}

ephemeral "aws_secretsmanager_secret_version" "api_key" {
  secret_id = "prod/api-key"       # read during the run only
}

resource "aws_db_instance" "main" {
  identifier          = "shop-prod"
  engine              = "postgres"
  instance_class      = "db.t4g.medium"
  allocated_storage   = 50
  username            = "shop"
  password_wo         = var.db_password   # write-only: sent, not stored
  password_wo_version = 2                 # bump to rotate
}
# State records password_wo_version, never the password itself.
